1
00:00:01,119 --> 00:00:04,680
"life would go on as it had always gone on."

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:08,680
That is, badly.

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:14,920
Apart from the disputes over the windmill, there was the question of the defense of the farm.

4
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:18,680
It was fully realized that though the human beings had been defeated in the

5
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:23,760
Battle of the Cowshed, they might make another and more determined attempt to

6
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,680
recapture the farm and reinstate Mr.

7
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,520
Jones.

8
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:33,159
They had all the more reason for doing so because the news of their defeat had

9
00:00:33,159 --> 00:00:37,760
spread across the countryside and made the animals on the neighboring farms

10
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,720
more restive than ever.

11
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:45,359
As usual, Snowball and Napoleon were in disagreement.

12
00:00:45,359 --> 00:00:50,840
According to Napoleon, what the animals must do was to procure firearms and

13
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:53,760
train themselves in the use of them.

14
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:59,239
According to Snowball, they must send out more and more pigeons and stir up

15
00:00:59,239 --> 00:01:03,359
rebellion among the animals on the other farms.

16
00:01:03,359 --> 00:01:09,319
The one argued that if they could not defend themselves, they were bound to be conquered.

17
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:14,079
The other argued that if rebellions happened everywhere, they would have no

18
00:01:14,079 --> 00:01:17,119
need to defend themselves.

19
00:01:17,119 --> 00:01:21,560
The animals listened first to Napoleon, then to Snowball,

20
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:25,439
and could not make up their minds which was right.

21
00:01:25,439 --> 00:01:32,039
Indeed, they always found themselves in agreement with the one who was speaking at the moment.

22
00:01:32,039 --> 00:01:36,239
At last the day came when Snowball's plans were completed.

23
00:01:36,239 --> 00:01:40,119
At the meeting on the following Sunday, the question of whether or not to begin

24
00:01:40,119 --> 00:01:43,560
work on the windmill was to be put to the vote.

25
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:48,399
When the animals had assembled in the big barn, Snowball stood up and, though

26
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:52,600
occasionally interrupted by bleating from the sheep, set forth his reasons

27
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,720
for advocating the building of the windmill.

28
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:58,359
Then Napoleon stood up to reply.

29
00:01:58,359 --> 00:02:03,000
He said very quietly that the windmill was nonsense and that he advised nobody

30
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,399
to vote for it and promptly sat down again.

31
00:02:06,399 --> 00:02:07,000
